steps.body:
A `for` loop does not have to move one index at a time. Change the update to jump, and change the start to shift which items you land on.

```javascript
for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i += 2) { }  // indexes 0, 2, 4, ...
for (let i = 1; i < arr.length; i += 2) { }  // indexes 1, 3, 5, ...
for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i += k) { }  // every k-th item
```

Keep the condition `i < arr.length` even when you jump. The last jump can land past the end, and the condition stops the loop before you read `undefined`.

To skip items by *value* instead of by position, test each item and `continue`. It ends the current pass and moves on to the next item.

```javascript
for (const item of arr) {
  if (item === 0) {
    continue;
  }
  // only nonzero items reach here
}
```

Collecting the visited items with `push` and printing them with `join(" ")` avoids a stray space at the end of the line.

example.code:
const letters = ["a", "b", "c", "d", "e", "f", "g"];
const vowels = ["a", "e", "i", "o", "u"];

const even = [];
for (let i = 0; i < letters.length; i += 2) {
  even.push(letters[i]);
}

const odd = [];
for (let i = 1; i < letters.length; i += 2) {
  odd.push(letters[i]);
}

const everyThird = [];
for (let i = 0; i < letters.length; i += 3) {
  everyThird.push(letters[i]);
}

const consonants = [];
for (const letter of letters) {
  if (vowels.includes(letter)) {
    continue;
  }
  consonants.push(letter);
}

console.log(`Even indexes: ${even.join(" ")}`);
console.log(`Odd indexes: ${odd.join(" ")}`);
console.log(`Every third: ${everyThird.join(" ")}`);
console.log(`No vowels: ${consonants.join(" ")}`);

